{"id": "EUVD-2026-102287", "enisaUuid": "a0daf23d-9a9b-3a6c-8d2c-c496f8cb9325", "description": "LightLLM through 1.2.0 contains a denial of service vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to crash the inference worker by supplying the internal pd_kv_trans_params field to the /generate endpoint. Attackers can send a single request whose parameters cause pickle.loads to fail in InferSamplingParams, killing the inference thread while /health stays up and all later requests hang until restart.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:24:32", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ModelTC/LightLLM/issues/1629", "https://github.com/ModelTC/lightllm/blob/v1.2.0/lightllm/server/api_lightllm.py#L37-L43", "https://github.com/ModelTC/lightllm/blob/v1.2.0/lightllm/server/core/objs/sampling_params.py#L356-L357", "https://github.com/ModelTC/lightllm/blob/v1.2.0/lightllm/server/router/model_infer/infer_batch.py#L484-L485", "https://github.com/ModelTC/LightLLM", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/lightllm-through-1.2.0-unauthenticated-dos-via-pd-kv-trans-params-deserialization"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mxm5-3g25-25c6", "CVE-2026-111160"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "25c9918d-bd39-312c-bbe6-e4ee0090fb51", "product": {"name": "LightLLM", "vendor": {"name": "ModelTC"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a3770013-86bb-3c31-9780-6b2b6fdce84a", "vendor": {"name": "ModelTC"}}], "isExploited": false}